WEBVTT

00:01.070 --> 00:03.140
I am Fujiwara no Kinto.

00:03.840 --> 00:06.280
Brilliant as always.

00:06.840 --> 00:09.310
So, there's a woman who's managed

00:09.310 --> 00:10.940
to attract my interest.

00:11.200 --> 00:13.700
The author of the Tale of Genji:

00:14.500 --> 00:16.160
To Shikibu.

00:17.190 --> 00:19.010
Gloom...

00:17.620 --> 00:19.620
Gloom

00:21.110 --> 00:23.770
I happen to like talented
women who are depressed.

00:23.770 --> 00:26.000
Or should I say "despondent"?

00:28.040 --> 00:36.470
Gloom

00:28.330 --> 00:30.140
They're fun to tease.

00:31.530 --> 00:34.120
I will address her as Hikaru
Genji's beloved wife,

00:34.120 --> 00:36.470
Murasaki no Ue.

00:37.480 --> 00:39.050
Hello, Murasaki-chan.

00:40.660 --> 00:42.490
You're not Hikaru Genji!

00:42.490 --> 00:44.270
Don't use that name!

00:49.690 --> 00:51.490
Why...

00:51.490 --> 00:53.440
You were acting out of character.

00:53.440 --> 00:57.160
Some people can get away with
sexual harassment, some can't.

00:58.000 --> 01:00.380
That wasn't sexual harassment!

01:00.380 --> 01:02.240
Plus, she was upset about something

01:02.240 --> 01:04.040
that was her own creation!

01:04.790 --> 01:07.570
Sounds like an excuse to me.

01:07.570 --> 01:09.530
If I said the same thing to her,

01:09.530 --> 01:11.460
she would have been happy.

01:11.460 --> 01:14.900
Tadanobu, what makes you say that?

01:14.900 --> 01:17.130
Let's see what happens, then.

01:18.290 --> 01:19.290
Hello.

01:20.770 --> 01:23.600
Where are you going, Murasaki-chan?

01:26.130 --> 01:28.000
Stop that...

01:28.000 --> 01:29.940
Don't call me Murasaki.

01:39.120 --> 01:44.880
No more can we hear the
sounds of the waterfall,

01:45.790 --> 01:57.300
but its legacy continues to spread.

01:47.200 --> 01:50.480
Kinto-sama, you need to head to work.

01:50.480 --> 01:52.580
There's a pile of paperwork
waiting for you.

01:53.910 --> 01:55.760
How long are you going
to dwell on that?

01:59.270 --> 02:01.190
You can be such a pain.

02:02.310 --> 02:03.640
I have no choice then...

02:09.000 --> 02:10.090
To Shikibu!

02:10.090 --> 02:12.360
Yukinari-sama?!

02:12.360 --> 02:14.190
Come with me!

02:14.190 --> 02:17.190
Follow my script!

02:17.450 --> 02:19.660
O-Okay...

02:23.410 --> 02:25.580
Hmm?  What's going on?

02:27.250 --> 02:30.140
I-I came to see how you were doing

02:30.140 --> 02:34.250
and offer my thanks.

02:34.250 --> 02:36.560
Thanks?  For what?

02:37.300 --> 02:39.600
Actually, I've decided to change

02:39.600 --> 02:44.220
my pen name from To Shikibu
to Murasaki Shikibu...

02:45.290 --> 02:49.560
I'm doing this because you called me

02:49.560 --> 02:54.570
by the name Murasaki a few days ago.

02:54.570 --> 02:58.820
The name has stuck in the palace,

02:58.820 --> 03:04.520
and the Tale of Genji has received
a popularity boost as a result.

03:04.520 --> 03:10.380
I-I wanted to thank you for
providing my new name.

03:11.900 --> 03:13.480
No need to thank me.

03:13.480 --> 03:16.750
I'm glad that I was
able to help you out!

03:20.530 --> 03:22.180
Back to work then!

03:25.470 --> 03:26.990
What happened to him?

03:26.990 --> 03:27.810
No idea.

05:01.170 --> 05:03.930
Hello, everyone!

05:03.930 --> 05:06.380
Fujiwara no Teika here.

05:07.300 --> 05:08.230
Test, test.

05:08.230 --> 05:09.050
Hello.

05:09.050 --> 05:10.910
Utsunomiya no Yoritsuna here.

05:11.460 --> 05:14.540
Has everyone heard of
the Tale of Genji?

05:14.540 --> 05:17.340
It's said to be the world's first novel,

05:17.340 --> 05:19.880
written around 1,000 years ago.

05:20.890 --> 05:24.010
Translated in over twenty
languages, including

05:24.010 --> 05:26.320
English, German, French, and Chinese,

05:26.320 --> 05:28.930
people all over the world
have read the book.

05:28.930 --> 05:40.810
Murasaki Shikibu

05:29.240 --> 05:33.220
The author of this novel
was Murasaki Shikibu,

05:33.790 --> 05:38.160
a woman who served in the palace
a little after Sei Shonagon.

05:38.160 --> 05:40.810
She must be very talented.

05:40.810 --> 05:44.820
Kaoriko and Fujiko

05:40.810 --> 05:44.820
Murasaki Shikibu

06:03.370 --> 06:06.700
Have you written more
yet, Shikibu-dono?

06:07.700 --> 06:10.340
Don't rush the poor girl.

06:10.340 --> 06:12.480
She must be having a slump.

06:17.850 --> 06:20.730
Honestly, I'm sick of writing...

06:21.460 --> 06:25.060
I can't stand fancy places.

06:25.700 --> 06:29.110
The story I wrote happened to be a hit,

06:29.460 --> 06:32.320
and I ended up in the palace

06:32.320 --> 06:34.700
as Empress Shoshi-sama's teacher...

06:35.670 --> 06:37.490
Oh, Shikibu.

06:37.950 --> 06:39.830
How is it going?

06:40.740 --> 06:44.170
Well, I'm having trouble
finding inspiration...

06:44.890 --> 06:46.290
That's fine.

06:46.290 --> 06:49.090
Take your time to create something beautiful.

06:49.670 --> 06:52.430
The Emperor is also looking
forward to the next part.

06:52.200 --> 06:55.010
Pressure

06:54.120 --> 06:55.010
Yes...

06:55.010 --> 06:57.290
Slump

06:55.930 --> 06:57.890
I can't write anything
because I'm in a slump.

06:57.290 --> 06:59.350
Expectation

06:57.890 --> 06:59.710
Everyone has high expectations.

06:59.710 --> 07:02.100
The pressure only lengthens my slump.

06:59.890 --> 07:01.770
Pressure

07:00.420 --> 07:01.770
Slump

07:00.890 --> 07:01.770
Slump

07:01.770 --> 07:03.420
Expectation

07:02.100 --> 07:04.240
Leading to even higher expectations.

07:03.400 --> 07:03.900
Pressure

07:03.400 --> 07:03.900
Slump

07:03.400 --> 07:03.900
Slump

07:03.900 --> 07:04.400
Expectation

07:04.240 --> 07:05.820
More pressure...

07:06.520 --> 07:10.110
A spiral of neverending despair!

07:11.400 --> 07:13.320
What am I supposed to write?

07:14.480 --> 07:16.670
In order to meet their expectations,

07:17.630 --> 07:20.660
I must provide entertainment
for this fancy palace?

07:21.810 --> 07:26.180
Write of romances that
only exist in dreams?

07:26.860 --> 07:28.210
I do not know.

07:28.210 --> 07:30.130
What should I write about?

07:30.820 --> 07:34.440
Besides, I never meant to
write such a long story.

07:35.020 --> 07:40.100
I just wanted to write about
illicit love and secret affairs.

07:42.050 --> 07:47.450
The love of Genji for his father's
wife, Lady Fujitsubo...

07:48.930 --> 07:52.040
Yes, for I am also in love...

07:54.850 --> 07:57.620
with someone beyond my reach.

07:59.860 --> 08:02.120
I wonder how she's doing now?

08:03.340 --> 08:07.090
My beautiful childhood
friend, Fujiko.

08:09.920 --> 08:11.240
Kaori!

08:12.090 --> 08:13.800
Fu-Fujiko...

08:14.380 --> 08:16.580
It's not safe up there, Fujiko!

08:16.580 --> 08:18.070
I'm perfectly fine!

08:18.070 --> 08:19.680
Here you go, Kaori!

08:20.890 --> 08:23.460
Fujiko was nimble as a small bird and

08:23.460 --> 08:25.480
stronger than anyone else I knew.

08:26.770 --> 08:29.930
I was always reading and

08:29.930 --> 08:32.410
spent every free moment I had studying...

08:33.480 --> 08:37.050
Oh, you've already learned
how to read Chinese poems?

08:37.500 --> 08:38.870
Father.

08:39.620 --> 08:43.510
I couldn't understand them
when I was your age.

08:43.510 --> 08:47.720
Your intelligence is marvelous.

08:53.850 --> 08:56.260
What are you doing?

08:56.630 --> 08:59.790
A mere girl reading Chinese poetry?

08:59.790 --> 09:01.670
You should be ashamed of yourself!

09:01.670 --> 09:04.450
Yeah, you're a total disgrace!

09:05.330 --> 09:06.340
A disgrace!

09:06.340 --> 09:08.230
Stupid girl!

09:08.230 --> 09:10.590
Ah, Kaoriko-dono already knows

09:10.590 --> 09:12.370
how to read Chinese poetry?

09:12.370 --> 09:14.450
I envy you.

09:14.450 --> 09:16.830
My child needs to work harder.

09:16.830 --> 09:21.570
However, knowledge is only
a burden for a woman.

09:24.610 --> 09:29.270
I regret that she wasn't born a man.

09:33.570 --> 09:34.640
Kaori?

09:35.390 --> 09:36.620
What's wrong?

09:37.690 --> 09:40.100
They said it was disgraceful for a girl

09:40.100 --> 09:41.620
to know Chinese poetry

09:41.620 --> 09:42.820
and laughed at me...

09:42.820 --> 09:44.290
What's that supposed to mean?

09:44.290 --> 09:46.600
I won't forgive anyone who makes you cry!

09:47.000 --> 09:49.480
Who was it?  I'll beat them up!

09:49.480 --> 09:50.860
It's okay!

09:50.860 --> 09:52.200
It's not okay!

09:52.200 --> 09:54.100
I won't forgive them until they
cry and say they're sorry!

09:54.100 --> 09:55.170
You can't!

09:55.170 --> 09:58.540
If you do that, they'll say
you're not like a girl, either!

09:59.630 --> 10:01.530
They can say whatever they want.

10:02.840 --> 10:04.500
Pull yourself together.

10:06.340 --> 10:10.420
I get to brag about how you're
smarter than the boys.

10:11.690 --> 10:13.570
That hurts, Fujiko...

10:16.310 --> 10:18.840
Hey, what poem were you
reading this time?

10:18.840 --> 10:20.390
A poem by Bai Juyi.

10:20.770 --> 10:23.110
A story about an Empress
more beautiful than any flower

10:23.110 --> 10:25.560
and the Emperor who was unable

10:25.560 --> 10:26.930
to prevent her death.

10:27.190 --> 10:30.040
Story?  A poem that told a story?

10:30.390 --> 10:33.460
Yes, a very sad story.

10:33.460 --> 10:34.820
Oh...

10:35.270 --> 10:36.450
I know!

10:36.450 --> 10:38.720
You should write a story, Kaori.

10:38.720 --> 10:39.480
Huh?

10:39.480 --> 10:42.240
No, I wouldn't know how.

10:42.240 --> 10:43.340
It'll be fine.

10:43.340 --> 10:45.640
You read books every day.

10:45.640 --> 10:47.200
You can write a story.

10:47.710 --> 10:49.600
I want to read your story!

10:49.600 --> 10:52.390
You can use a pen name, okay?

10:58.370 --> 10:59.920
A story...

10:59.920 --> 11:02.280
Write a story for Fujiko...

11:14.150 --> 11:15.280
Wow.

11:15.280 --> 11:15.730
Huh?

11:15.730 --> 11:18.390
You're amazing, Kaori!
This is really good!

11:18.390 --> 11:19.570
Really?

11:19.570 --> 11:21.290
I can't believe you were
able to write this!

11:21.290 --> 11:25.200
You're amazing, Kaori!  Amazing!

11:25.790 --> 11:28.920
You're a good student,
and you can write stories, too!

11:28.920 --> 11:30.940
You could beat any man!

11:31.900 --> 11:34.090
Right, promise me something.

11:34.090 --> 11:35.130
Promise?

11:35.550 --> 11:39.430
Yes, between my brawn and your brains,

11:39.430 --> 11:40.920
we can defeat any man.

11:41.490 --> 11:43.890
We'll laugh in the faces of
the people who think

11:43.890 --> 11:45.440
women can't do anything.

11:47.220 --> 11:48.420
What is it?

11:48.420 --> 11:49.710
Nothing.

11:50.170 --> 11:51.360
Promise?

11:52.480 --> 11:53.770
Promise.

11:55.050 --> 11:58.180
Fujiko was the only one who
accepted me for who I was,

11:58.620 --> 11:59.970
who said good things about me.

12:01.020 --> 12:02.650
Fujiko and I...

12:02.650 --> 12:03.740
Me and Fujiko...

12:04.320 --> 12:05.670
Fujiko was all I needed.

12:06.310 --> 12:08.330
As long as I had Fujiko by my side,

12:08.330 --> 12:10.830
there was nothing else I wanted.

12:12.850 --> 12:15.500
What?  You're getting married?

12:15.500 --> 12:17.380
Looks like it.

12:17.380 --> 12:20.280
It was a good offer, so I took it.

12:20.280 --> 12:21.220
I see...

12:21.220 --> 12:23.800
Oh, what's with that look?

12:23.800 --> 12:25.880
I'm not getting married because

12:25.880 --> 12:27.470
my parents forced me into it.

12:27.850 --> 12:28.870
But...

12:28.870 --> 12:31.700
I just decided to try a different angle.

12:31.700 --> 12:33.330
What are you trying to accomplish?

12:33.330 --> 12:35.010
At this age, I can no longer beat men

12:35.010 --> 12:37.440
when it comes to brute strength.

12:37.440 --> 12:41.820
You can still use your writing
to compete with men.

12:42.780 --> 12:46.510
I was thinking about
how I could beat men

12:46.510 --> 12:48.330
when I don't have any useful skills...

12:49.360 --> 12:51.400
but I have my beauty!

12:51.850 --> 12:55.360
I realized I could put
men under my spell.

12:55.360 --> 12:57.820
So, I'm getting married!

12:57.820 --> 12:59.350
Silly Fujiko...

13:00.600 --> 13:02.480
You never show any weakness.

13:03.400 --> 13:05.310
You probably couldn't
refuse because it would

13:05.310 --> 13:06.680
put your parents in a bad position.

13:07.430 --> 13:10.690
Despite everything you say,
you're a faithful daughter.

13:11.750 --> 13:15.070
Oh, I don't plan on sitting
in the house all day.

13:15.070 --> 13:18.270
My future husband seems to
understand the palace workings,

13:18.920 --> 13:21.160
so I can use him as a stepping stone.

13:21.830 --> 13:25.780
She's always optimistic, no matter
how painful the situation.

13:26.620 --> 13:29.540
I love the inner strength in
you that I don't have.

13:30.380 --> 13:32.290
I love you so much, Fujiko...

13:34.120 --> 13:37.000
I'm proud to call you my best friend.

13:40.420 --> 13:42.210
However, I do have one regret.

13:43.630 --> 13:46.960
Once I'm married,
I'll be leaving the capital.

13:46.960 --> 13:47.850
What?

13:47.850 --> 13:50.390
My future husband is being
assigned to a new post.

13:52.560 --> 13:54.140
That can't be...

13:54.590 --> 13:55.350
Kaori...

13:58.840 --> 14:00.350
Fujiko?

14:01.180 --> 14:03.650
I wanted to be with you forever.

14:04.910 --> 14:08.740
If you were a man, I could
have married you instead.

14:10.180 --> 14:11.720
Indeed...

14:13.250 --> 14:17.020
Why wasn't I born a man?

14:18.310 --> 14:23.190
Why can't I be the one
to make her happy?

14:24.480 --> 14:29.600
When I'm the one who
needs her the most,

14:29.600 --> 14:31.880
who loves her most in this world.

14:37.360 --> 14:40.680
It wasn't long before Fujiko
followed her husband

14:40.680 --> 14:42.400
and left the capital...

14:43.430 --> 14:45.790
Soon after, I also married,

14:46.460 --> 14:48.200
but my husband passed away.

14:49.090 --> 14:54.290
Now, I serve the current
Empress, Shoshi-sama.

14:56.780 --> 15:00.100
I haven't seen Fujiko since she left.

15:01.640 --> 15:04.960
Fujiko, please return to the capital.

15:06.250 --> 15:08.940
I miss you, I miss you so much.

15:11.010 --> 15:12.030
Fujiko...

15:26.050 --> 15:30.530
Oh, your husband has been
assigned to the countryside?

15:31.210 --> 15:34.280
Yes, he's finally received
a slight promotion.

15:34.280 --> 15:35.790
Will you be accompanying him?

15:35.790 --> 15:38.620
Absolutely not.
He'll be going by himself.

15:38.620 --> 15:40.430
Won't you be lonely?

15:40.430 --> 15:41.670
Not at all.

15:41.670 --> 15:44.690
I care much more about my job here.

15:44.690 --> 15:46.480
So you say now,

15:46.480 --> 15:48.900
but don't blame me when you
cry yourself to sleep at night.

15:48.900 --> 15:50.470
What are you babbling about?

15:52.080 --> 15:53.880
Oh, yes.

15:53.880 --> 15:54.980
Shikibu-dono.

15:54.980 --> 15:55.760
Yes?

15:56.680 --> 16:00.100
About the childhood friend
you mentioned before.

16:01.560 --> 16:03.290
Her husband's assignment has ended

16:03.290 --> 16:05.390
and he has returned to the capital.

16:06.210 --> 16:08.070
Fujiko is back in the capital?

16:08.070 --> 16:10.320
Oh, you didn't know?

16:10.320 --> 16:11.950
Y-Yes...

16:11.950 --> 16:14.570
Then you should go see her.

16:14.570 --> 16:18.540
Her husband has been
named governor of Kai.

16:18.740 --> 16:20.020
What?!

16:20.020 --> 16:23.030
His entire family will be leaving soon.

16:27.510 --> 16:30.420
Why didn't you let me know, Fujiko?!

16:30.890 --> 16:33.990
When I...  When I miss you so much!

16:36.000 --> 16:38.180
Oh, Fujiko...

16:41.610 --> 16:45.400
I'm still spending all
of my time studying.

16:46.010 --> 16:50.730
As I promised, I can compete
with the men with my writing.

16:51.100 --> 16:55.860
I've written a story that
was praised by the Emperor.

16:56.540 --> 17:01.140
Are you still fighting a lot?

17:02.780 --> 17:06.360
Fujiko, there are so many
things I want to tell you.

17:07.520 --> 17:10.410
I...  I want to see you!

17:23.630 --> 17:24.710
Fujiko.

17:27.340 --> 17:28.310
Fujiko!

17:48.290 --> 17:49.100
Huh?

17:52.990 --> 17:54.650
Was it someone else?

17:55.410 --> 17:58.290
No, that was Fujiko!

17:58.890 --> 18:01.560
I would recognize her anywhere!

18:03.990 --> 18:05.610
Why...

18:07.200 --> 18:10.080
Why, Fujiko?

18:30.840 --> 18:33.840
Madam, I have a letter.

18:34.790 --> 18:36.750
From a woman named Kaori.

18:39.770 --> 18:44.300
Long last we meet, only
for me to leave hurriedly,

18:45.070 --> 18:46.970
for I could not recognize you,

18:46.970 --> 18:49.050
like the moon hidden behind the clouds.

18:50.740 --> 18:53.230
Was it truly you that I saw,

18:54.010 --> 18:56.480
like the moon on a cloudy night?

18:57.620 --> 18:59.320
I thought I'd found you,

18:59.320 --> 19:00.800
but then you were hidden from me again.

19:05.470 --> 19:06.710
Mother.

19:07.820 --> 19:09.590
Goro peed his pants.

19:11.640 --> 19:14.250
Oh, dear.  What are you doing?

19:14.250 --> 19:17.270
Father?  Where's Father?

19:17.270 --> 19:21.290
I know!  He went to see his lover.

19:21.290 --> 19:23.520
What's a lover?

19:23.520 --> 19:26.180
You don't know?  You're dumb.

19:27.360 --> 19:28.510
Shut up!

19:31.940 --> 19:34.930
Oh, sorry.  That was my fault.

19:34.930 --> 19:36.030
Now, now.

19:37.020 --> 19:39.240
I can't see you now, Kaori...

19:40.310 --> 19:43.850
We're too far apart now.

19:45.020 --> 19:52.210
I can't let you see what I've become.

19:52.880 --> 19:56.170
A woman who meekly obeys men.

20:03.120 --> 20:06.420
Yes, between my brawn and your brains,

20:06.420 --> 20:08.490
we can defeat any man.

20:10.190 --> 20:14.480
Was I the only one
honoring our promise?

20:16.300 --> 20:17.970
Has Fujiko turned her back

20:17.970 --> 20:21.290
on the determination
we once shared?

20:24.650 --> 20:28.270
No, her feelings have not changed.

20:29.180 --> 20:34.540
However, she isn't allowed
to live as she wishes,

20:36.300 --> 20:37.550
because she's a woman.

20:39.120 --> 20:41.040
Because she was born a woman...

20:50.340 --> 20:52.140
I finally know

20:53.550 --> 20:56.610
what I should write about
in the Tale of Genji.

20:57.360 --> 20:58.180
No,

20:59.120 --> 21:00.610
this is what I want to write.

21:03.780 --> 21:08.110
This will not be a story
about glorious palace life

21:08.110 --> 21:10.450
or dreamy romance...

21:12.750 --> 21:14.290
This story is about a woman's strength.

21:15.490 --> 21:18.570
The graceful strength that women possess.

21:19.650 --> 21:24.250
If I keep writing, Fujiko may
read this story one day.

21:26.190 --> 21:28.950
I want to show Fujiko.

21:32.320 --> 21:35.110
As she is on the verge of crumbling

21:35.110 --> 21:38.010
in a world where women have no freedom,

21:38.730 --> 21:41.050
I can show her the
strength women have.

21:48.050 --> 21:49.230
It'll be fine.

21:49.230 --> 21:50.870
You can write a story.

21:51.840 --> 21:53.780
I want to read your story!

21:54.500 --> 21:56.590
You're amazing, Kaori!

21:56.590 --> 21:58.930
I can't believe you were
able to write this!

21:58.930 --> 22:01.800
You're amazing, Kaori!  Amazing!

22:02.620 --> 22:03.510
Fujiko.

22:04.240 --> 22:07.380
I will send these feelings to you.

22:09.330 --> 22:11.180
By using

22:12.470 --> 22:14.970
the storytelling that you praised.

22:20.880 --> 22:23.820
